issue.description:
Simplify the accepted UI Effects behavior for surface-style Tabs.

The current Tactile effect applies an adjustable tactile treatment to active surface-style Tabs. This ticket changes that model so Tabs receive only one fixed, subtle container-level enhancement, while the Strength control applies only to Secondary Buttons.

## Overall direction

When UI Effects = Tactile:

* Secondary Buttons keep the accepted adjustable tactile treatment;
* the Strength control continues to affect Secondary Buttons;
* surface-style Tabs no longer receive the adjustable tactile recipe;
* active TabsTrigger styling returns to the normal/default shadcn selected-state appearance;
* the TabsList container receives only a subtle fixed ring:
  * `ring-1 ring-ring/20`

When UI Effects = Off:

* Secondary Buttons are flat;
* Tabs use their normal default shadcn appearance;
* TabsList has no extra UI Effects ring;
* Strength remains disabled/de-emphasized as already accepted.

## 1. Remove tactile treatment from active tab triggers

Remove the custom/accepted tactile effect currently applied directly to the active surface-style `TabsTrigger`.

Requirements:

* preserve shadcn default selected-state styling;
* preserve inactive trigger styling;
* preserve keyboard navigation;
* preserve selected-state semantics;
* preserve focus-visible behavior;
* preserve current Tabs sizing and layout;
* do not add a replacement shadow/highlight recipe to the active trigger.

The active tab should look like the normal accepted shadcn active tab.

## 2. Apply fixed ring to TabsList container

When UI Effects = Tactile, apply only this container-level treatment to accepted surface-style Tabs:

`ring-1 ring-ring/20`

Requirements:

* apply to the `TabsList` container, not individual triggers;
* use the existing semantic `ring` token;
* keep the opacity fixed at 20%;
* preserve existing TabsList background, radius, spacing, and geometry;
* do not add extra shadow, highlight, inset, border, or glow as part of this ticket.

This fixed ring is the entire UI Effects treatment for Tabs.

## 3. Strength affects Secondary Buttons only

Update the UI Effects behavior so the Strength control no longer changes Tabs in any way.

Strength should affect only the accepted Secondary Button tactile recipe.

Requirements:

* changing Strength updates Secondary Button tactility;
* TabsList `ring-ring/20` remains visually unchanged at every Strength value;
* active tab styling remains unchanged at every Strength value;
* no hidden tab-specific strength mapping remains.

The UI model should make this separation explicit in implementation and tests.

## 4. Preserve Secondary Button tactile behavior

Do not redesign the accepted Secondary Button tactile treatment in this ticket.

Preserve:

* subtle internal illumination/light wash;
* restrained depth;
* semantic edge/ring treatment;
* existing Strength mapping;
* light/dark behavior;
* keyboard/focus/disabled semantics.

This ticket is primarily a Tabs simplification and Strength-scope correction.

## 5. UI Effects semantics

Accepted behavior after this ticket:

### Effect = Off

* Secondary Buttons: flat
* surface-style Tabs: normal shadcn appearance
* no extra TabsList ring
* Strength disabled/de-emphasized

### Effect = Tactile

* Secondary Buttons: tactile and controlled by Strength
* surface-style Tabs:
  * normal shadcn trigger appearance
  * `TabsList` gets `ring-1 ring-ring/20`
  * unaffected by Strength

Line/minimal Tabs remain excluded as before.

## 6. Theme / state boundaries

Prefer preserving the current Theme v3 UI Effects persisted shape unless a narrow implementation cleanup is needed.

Do not:

* introduce a new persisted Tabs strength field;
* add per-target toggles;
* add a new effect family;
* introduce Theme v4;
* change mutation count unless the accepted closed operation contract genuinely requires a narrow update;
* change import/export semantics beyond what is required to preserve current Off/Tactile + Strength behavior.

If the current renderer or persisted model assumes Tabs use Strength, remove that coupling without expanding schema.

Preserve:

* history;
* dirty state;
* reset;
* save/reload;
* import/export;
* Design Command boundaries;
* public registry.

## 7. Scope

Apply this to accepted **surface-style Tabs** that participate in UI Effects.

Do not change:

* line/minimal Tabs;
* unrelated tab variants;
* Button variants other than preserving Secondary behavior;
* Inputs;
* Cards;
* other primitives;
* Workbench navigation semantics;
* tab layout/width behavior.

No new dependency or network behavior.

## 8. Verification

Verify:

* UI Effects Off:
  * no extra TabsList ring;
  * normal shadcn active/inactive tab appearance;
  * Secondary Buttons flat;
  * Strength disabled/de-emphasized.
* UI Effects Tactile:
  * TabsList receives exactly the intended subtle semantic ring treatment;
  * active trigger no longer receives the tactile recipe;
  * Secondary Buttons remain tactile;
  * Strength changes Secondary Button appearance;
  * Strength does not change Tabs visually.

Also verify:

* light/dark mode;
* keyboard navigation;
* focus-visible behavior;
* selected-state semantics;
* narrow/wide responsive layouts;
* existing Theme v3/history/reset/import-export behavior;
* no regression to Design Command, mutation boundary, or registry.

## Acceptance

* Active surface-style TabsTrigger uses the normal/default shadcn selected-state styling.
* No adjustable tactile shadow/highlight treatment remains on active tab triggers.
* When UI Effects = Tactile, TabsList receives `ring-1 ring-ring/20`.
* When UI Effects = Off, that extra TabsList ring is absent.
* Strength affects Secondary Buttons only.
* Changing Strength does not alter TabsList or TabsTrigger appearance.
* Secondary Button tactile behavior remains materially unchanged.
* Line/minimal Tabs remain unaffected.
* No Theme v4, new dependency, network behavior, per-target toggle, or unrelated product change is introduced.
